The legal text is not Lexifina's. It was copied by script from the Gibraltar Laws website
(https://www.gibraltarlaws.gov.gi), published by the Government of Gibraltar, and keeps the source's terms:

- The PDFs carry the line "(c) Government of Gibraltar (www.gibraltarlaws.gov.gi)". The site states no licence.
- Its copyright-and-disclaimer page (https://www.gibraltarlaws.gov.gi/copyright-and-disclaimer) says: "Please note
  that it cannot be guaranteed that a document available on-line exactly reproduces an officially adopted text.
  Only Government of Gibraltar legislation published in paper editions of the Gibraltar Gazette and Supplements is
  deemed authentic."

Credit the source as: (c) Government of Gibraltar (www.gibraltarlaws.gov.gi), as published at gibraltarlaws.gov.gi,
with changes to layout only (white space and page furniture). The Gibraltar Gazette is the authentic text.
